d4_codex_review: 2026-10-26 - read-only Codex review of medfit 9599608 (+#341/#342/#355), nothing run, nothing changed: no high-severity defect; compare_lr/anova handle the new class safely. Open design findings for the medfit maintainer: (1) moderate, a losing-branch covariance failure invalidates a union whose winner has valid covariance (R/sem-fit.R:391-402); (2) moderate, every .sem_vcov() error is retained as LR evidence, not only the improper-null case (R/sem-fit.R:189,204; R/sem-mbco.R:197); (3) low, root attribution is first-in-branch-order, #355 pins it; (4) low, retention checks consistency, not forgery. Also: NEWS migration note for simpleError handlers. Unverified: tests not run, b45cb4c18 absent from local medfit objects, no natural negative-variance fixture. D4 gate stays open; no fix authorized.
d4_repro: 2026-10-26 - authorized read-only repro of Codex findings 1-2 against the medfit test-d4-closure worktree (no medfit writes; script in session scratchpad). CONFIRMED 1: on the memory_exp union (winner = branch 2) a planted .sem_vcov failure in the losing branch alone raises medfit_sem_covariance_error and returns no fit (winner-only failure also raises). CONFIRMED 2: mbco_sem() retains the null with 2 warnings for 'computationally singular', 'negative variance' and 'out of memory' alike; nothing separates an improper-null failure from any other error. Both match the code comments (deliberate: no fit when the union is incomplete), so defect-vs-policy is still the medfit owner's ruling. Planted failures only; no natural negative-variance fixture. D4 gate stays open.
d4_owner_ruling: 2026-10-26 - medfit author ruling via medfit-oct-25 (second Codex pass rated finding 2 HIGH, vs main). (b) NARROW: .sem_vcov() raises a new typed class for medfit's own covariance diagnostics (singular/non-PD information, negative variance); only it is retained as LR evidence (sem-fit.R, .sem_retain_covariance); any other error incl. OOM fails closed; tests cover allowed and refused classes. (a) KEEP union invalidation on a losing-branch covariance failure (intended, fails closed; ADR, no code change, revisit after (b)). Pending: medfit PR to dev (link to follow). D4 gate and T5 stay OPEN; no medfit change made from here.
